```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping(
        path = "/orders",
        produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
class OrderController {
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    OrderView find(@PathVariable long id) {
        return new OrderView(id, "Keyboard");
    }

    @PostMapping(consumes = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
    OrderView create(@RequestBody CreateOrderRequest request) {
        return new OrderView(42, request.item());
    }
}
```

The final routes are `GET /orders/{id}` and `POST /orders`. The class-level `produces` condition applies to both methods, while only POST declares a JSON request body through `consumes`.
